<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Empress Xiaozhuangwen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1613">1613</a>–<a href="/years/1688">1688</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Bumbutai, Consort Zhuang, Empress Dowager Zhaosheng, Grand Empress Dowager Zhaosheng</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Empress Xiaozhuangwen, born Bumbutai of the Khorchin Mongol Borjigit clan, was a consort of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchu</a> ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-taiji">Hong Taiji</a>, whom she married in 1625 as one of his several wives. Her son Fulin became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shunzhi-emperor">Shunzhi Emperor</a> in 1643, and she was honoured as Empress Dowager Zhaosheng, then as Grand Empress Dowager under her grandson, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kangxi-emperor">Kangxi Emperor</a>. She took charge of the young Kangxi Emperor's upbringing and in 1669 helped him remove the regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oboi">Oboi</a> from power. Respected for her political wisdom, she died in 1688 and was named Empress Xiaozhuangwen posthumously, though she never held the rank of empress consort in her lifetime.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/empress-xiaozhuangwen.jpg" alt="Empress Xiaozhuangwen" width="330" height="694" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Imperial_Portrait_of_Empress_Xiao_Zhuang_Wen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
